# Trivy misconfiguration baseline for terraform/.
# Established when the pre-commit hook migrated from the deprecated tfsec to
# trivy (tfsec could not parse the Terraform 1.5 `check` blocks in testnet.tf).
# Entries are either intentional architecture (kept, with rationale) or
# pre-existing findings queued for the validation-fixes pass (marked TODO).

# --- Intentional architecture ---

# Public-facing ALB fronted by WAF (waf.tf); exposure is the design.
AVD-AWS-0053

# HTTP listener forwards only when no certificate_arn is configured; with a
# cert it 301-redirects to HTTPS (alb.tf). Production sets certificate_arn.
AVD-AWS-0054

# ECS tasks need unrestricted egress to reach ECR, Stellar Horizon/RPC,
# Twilio, FCM, and other external APIs; scoping would require VPC endpoints
# plus an allowlist that breaks the bridge's outbound integrations.
AVD-AWS-0104

# Public subnets host only the ALB and NAT gateways; auto-assign public IPs
# is required there. Services run in private subnets.
AVD-AWS-0164

# ALB access-log delivery does not support SSE-KMS; the alb_logs bucket must
# use SSE-S3 (AES256). Backup buckets use SSE-S3 by choice (no CMK to manage).
AVD-AWS-0132

# The jobs topics are encrypted with the AWS-managed SNS key (alias/aws/sns);
# a customer-managed key is not worth the key-policy and rotation surface for
# internal job-dispatch payloads. Same trade-off as AVD-AWS-0132 above.
AVD-AWS-0136

# (SNS/SQS at-rest encryption AVD-AWS-0095/0096 and ALB header-dropping
# AVD-AWS-0052 were fixed rather than ignored; the alerts topic in
# monitoring.tf carries a scoped inline trivy:ignore instead.)
